-- | OpenZeppelin Pausable - the interface for an emergency-stop switch on a
-- Daml template.
--
-- The implementing template holds a `paused` flag and declares an
-- `interface instance Pausable` whose view reports it. The guards and the
-- failure statuses live in the `openzeppelin-pausable-v1` package, module
-- `OpenZeppelin.PausableV1`.
--
-- The flag is a field of the contract being exercised, so a guard reads it
-- from the contract it runs on. The consumer decides who may pause:
-- authorization lives in the controller and body of the consumer's flip
-- choice, which creates the successor with the flag changed, so any model
-- fits, from a single party to a role grant, an M-of-N approval, or a
-- timelock.
--
-- The template's signatories can always archive the contract and create it
-- again with any flag value, outside the flip choice. A pause authority model
-- holds only when every signatory is part of that model or is trusted with
-- the flag.
--
-- The switch is per contract and applies to new transactions: a gated choice
-- refuses to start while the flag is set.
module OpenZeppelin.Api.PausableV1 where

-- | The view of a `Pausable` contract.
data PausableView = PausableView with
    paused : Bool
      -- ^ `True` while the contract is paused.
  deriving (Eq, Show)

-- | The emergency-stop switch, implemented by any template that holds a
-- `paused` flag:
--
-- ```
-- interface instance Pausable for Vault where
--   view = PausableView with paused
-- ```
--
-- The interface defines no choice: the implementing template's own choices
-- flip the flag. The guards in `OpenZeppelin.PausableV1` raise the failure
-- statuses.
interface Pausable where
  viewtype PausableView
